WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.770
M...Master Vector, what in the world are these?

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.350
Those are Numbers I made.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.940
Fake Numbers, to put it bluntly.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.400
Fake Numbers?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.990
Correct. And when I scatter them across the Human World...

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:33.500
Oooh! These fake Numbers have such a <i>bravo</i> effect!

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.630
I want you to spread them throughout the Human World.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.640
And also get your hands on Kaito's and Ryouga's Numbers.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.260
Leave it to me!

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.850
I'll definitely get their Numbers!

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.850
Urgh... It hurts...!

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.730
That's much better.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.980
Listening? This is your <i>last</i> chance.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:59.150
I... I understand, master.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.990
This time, I'll make sure...

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.920
Guess I got no choice. I'm giving you one last chance.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.380
But if you don't screw this up, maybe I'll make you one of the Seven Emperors.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.630
Me... One of the Seven Emperors!?

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.550
Yeah.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.260
I-I thank you for your mercy!

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.510
Kaito snatched one of your friend's Numbers, right?

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:32.270
And even an incompetent buffoon like <i>you</i>
 can win if you use <i>that</i> card.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:00.170
This will be the end of Earth and Astral World.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.050
But as things are, we still haven't gotten our hands on the Numeron Code...

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.220
I don't care.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.350
Even if Astral World disappears, I can finally achieve my goal.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.650
<i>The riots that started this morning show no signs of stopping.</i>

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.120
Another riot, huh?

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.330
They've been happening all over in the last few days.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:33.330
And they've also been happening here in Heartland.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.000
But wh-eow all of a sudden?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.090
It seems to be due to Numbers.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.500
Numbers?

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:48.510
Yes. I don't how they got them, but those who have them seem to be the source of these messes.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.180
Also, it looks like there's around one million of them...

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.390
- One million Numbers...!?
 - Meow can that be?!

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.850
It's impossible.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:56.850
Then it's got to be...

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.110
The Barians.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.110
Yes.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:02.570
None of you picked up any weird looking Numbers, right?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.610
Ne-ope!

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.240
I haven't even seen one.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:05.820
Nope.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.530
More importantly, what happened to Yuma, or not?

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:12.580
We can't use the Comm systems here right now.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.830
If this is right...

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.120
It looks like Big Brother V has finally returned.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:04:00.610
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.660
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:11.120
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:14.670
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.550
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:25.890
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:29.100
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.980
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.610
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.690
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:48.160
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.770
The Dimensional Gateway you sent Yuma through closed?

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.730
So what happened to Yuma?

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.490
I don't know.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:12.780
"Sign of the World's Collapse!!
 Mr. Heartland's Grand Revolt"

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.160
Yuma isn't coming back, or not?

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.660
Oh no...! He can't have...!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.170
How...?! How could you leave Yuma behind, or not?!

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.580
To do something something like that, or not...!

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.580
To... Tokunosuke, quit it!

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.130
Yuma's okay.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:29.920
Yuma'll definitely come back to us.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.590
Kotori-<i>san</i>...

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:35.300
He's gonna come back safe and sound no matter what.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.060
Yeah.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.060
Yup.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.270
And with Astral by his side.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.230
- Yeah.
 - Yeah.

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.190
Yeah.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.980
<i>Beautiful... beautiful!</i>

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.360
<i>What a truly beautiful friendship you kids have.</i>

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:53.820
You...!

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.780
Mr. Heartland!

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:02.710
<i>But I have to inform you that you're never going to see Yuma Tsukumo again.</i>

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.420
Now, kids, you should come outside!

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.630
<i>Bonjour, everyone.</i>

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:16.010
I'd love to sit and chat about old times,
 but I don't think you'd enjoy that.

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:17.350
Right, Kaito?

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.850
Heartland.... You sonnuva bitch!

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.350
Now, everyone, if you'll look over there!

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:31.990
Wha... What is that!?

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.780
IT'S SHOW TIME!

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:48.290
Barian... Barian... Barian...

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.500
What the...?

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.220
M-My body...

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.010
...feels heavy...

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.760
There's a change in the Spatial Mass!

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:02.020
That pillar of light is the energy of the Barian World!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.730
What did you say!?

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:06.100
Could it be...

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.730
...that you're trying to unite our world and the Barian's?!

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.150
Bingo!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:14.070
And your door prize is an eternal trip to the afterlife!

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.490
And you get a group invitation!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.870
You sunnova... how the hell did you find us!?

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:28.330
That's all thanks to the Numbers we've been handing out all over the world.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.710
What?

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:34.760
People who are greedier than most can't hide their greed.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:39.470
They're attracted to the hearts of <i>weaklings</i>, you see.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:44.470
And those who have one give off a special frequency.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.440
Simply put, I followed it here.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.900
Then someone here has a Number on them!?

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.440
Hey, you punks!

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.990
I thought you kids said you had none of those damned things!

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.900
Hey, don't look at me!

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:57.950
Nor me!

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.240
It's ne-ot me!

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.620
Tokunosuke-<i>kun</i>?

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.330
Tch. Idiot.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.340
Why did you...?

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:14.300
I... I... picked it up.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:21.180
I figured if I had this I could be stronger at Dueling... I... I...

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.640
I thought I might be able to help Yuma...

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.850
I...I'm always so useless, or not.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.520
So... So...

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.320
You wanted to help!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:39.990
Such good intentions paved the road to Hell, I'm afraid.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.490
How splendid!

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:45.290
And soon, the entire planet will be swallowed up!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.540
Into the Barian World!

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.830
And those with their hands on the Numbers we gave out...

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:55.800
...can no longer control their desires and emotions.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.260
They'll turn into dark energy.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:02.180
And get sucked up into the pipe connecting this world and the Barian World.

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:07.060
Thus becoming the power source that'll draw our worlds in different dimensions together!

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:12.940
Correct. What I'm trying to do is fuse both worlds together.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.150
So that's it!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.900
And when the riots were happening across the planet,

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:19.360
Tokunosuke-<i>kun</i> did seem to get unusually angry!

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.110
And what the hell were you trying to get out of doing that?!

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.070
Well, that's...

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:25.780
Correct.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:32.960
By consuming and fusing with our world, the Barians will be able to attack the Astral World like Haruto did.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.960
How dare you steal my lines!

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:42.930
And if our world is consumed by the Barian's,
 that'll be the end of us.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.350
- Tokunosuke!
 - Tokunosuke-<i>kun</i>!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.020
And you'll become another human sacrifice as well!

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.100
<i>Adieu</i>!

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.270
Tokunosuke!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.730
No! Tokunosuke-<i>kun</i>!

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:05.160
Just relax. You're all going to vanish soon anyways.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.370
Along with the entire world.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:14.370
However, hand over all the Numbers you kids have first.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:17.000
Then you'll have to take mine by force!

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.750
Kaito...

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:25.390
Even if you didn't say that just now, I had every intent of tearing yours out with my own two hands!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:30.220
Because you're an ungrateful brat who stabbed the Number Hunters in the back despite everything they did for you!

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:33.940
The idea of owing you a favor... it makes my skin crawl.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.690
And I don't remember become the subordinate of some shitty worm like you!

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.860
Shut up, shut up, SHUT UP~!

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.690
FINE, LET'S DUEL!

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:45.740
That's just what I wanted! Duel Mode! Photon Change!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:53.080
Today, I'll send you to Hell!

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:54.460
KAITO!

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:06.510
Duel!!

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:22.110
It hurts, doesn't it, Kaito?

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:26.610
This world is turning into the Barian World.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:31.240
In other words, the entire planet
has the same effect as the Barian's Field.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:36.750
In other words, it's a Duel where you'll feel real pain!

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.500
What a <i>convenient</i> handicap for your opponent.

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:45.010
Then, to make up for your handicap, I'll let you attack first!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:47.220
It's my turn! Draw!

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.010
I Summon Infection Fly!

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:00.900
And then I activate the Magic Card,
 Hell Multiplication, from my hand!

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:08.860
When I have a Level Two Monster on my field, I can Special Summon all copies of that Monster from my hand!

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:12.490
Appear, my two Infection Flies!

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:17.830
And then I activate Infection Fly's effect!

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:22.290
I can double the Level of all Monsters.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.170
And he's got two more of that same monster on the field...

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:27.260
So that means... That effect'll...

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.630
That's right!

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:38.730
I can double the Levels of my monsters using the effects of my Infection Flies two more times! I double 'em again!

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.360
Double! Double!

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:48.320
To get three Level Eight Monsters just like that...

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:50.320
Now, here I come, Kaito.

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:53.870
I Overlay these three Level Eight Infection Flies!

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:59.160
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:01.120
Xyz Summon!

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.300
Appear now, Number 1!

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:18.730
Amazing Lord of the Flies, Dark wings that flap with a fantastic roar! Infection Baal Zeboul!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.520
That's Number 1?!

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.910
It looks like you're all too stunned to talk!

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.740
It's Number One of all Numbers!

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:36.160
NUMBER ONE!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.120
So what?

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:43.580
Speaking right after I said you were too stunned to speak!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.170
Number 1 was Summoned?

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:52.720
With this, my preparations are complete.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:56.140
One is the beginning of everything.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.560
The Apex of the Numbers!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.060
You should get on your knees and grovel!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.520
Number 1 in Attendance! Number 1!

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.020
Nonsense.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:07.400
Why you...!

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:09.690
I'm gonna beat fear into you!

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:12.650
When Infection Baal Zeboul is Summoned...

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:16.700
...a Monster is sent from my opponent's Extra Deck to the Graveyard.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:20.910
Shadow Mosquito should be in your Extra Deck.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.420
Shadow Mosquito?

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.960
The Number you took from Mosquito Ninja.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.380
What the heck?

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:34.840
I send that Number 2, Shadow Mosquito, to the Graveyard.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.980
That's it!

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:54.490
The Numbers you idiots took from my Barian assassins are <i>all a buncha fakes</i>!

00:14:55.030 --> 00:15:03.910
By letting them take root in your decks, the energy load of the Barian's Field is a buncha times greater when they come out!

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:07.580
You friggin' humans won't be able to take that much damage!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.920
How's that, Kaito?!

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.050
<i>What's... with these shocks and this pain?</i>

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:20.930
Things are gettin' i<i>interesting</i>!

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:26.600
Huh? That light... That's the signal for the Seven Barian Emperors to gather?

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:30.770
I set one card and end my turn!

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:34.650
Oh? You got back up?

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.910
It would be boring if you didn't.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.200
It wouldn't do for it to end like that.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:43.240
Just how hard do you think I worked to make your father's, Faker's, dream a reality?!

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:49.710
You're just some shitty slimeball cat burglar wanted by the police...that my father used as a cover!

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:52.710
Y-You little shit...!

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:54.050
Cat burglar?

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:54.630
A sneaky thief.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.630
My turn! Draw!

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:02.350
I activate the Ritual Spell, Descent of Quantum Dragon, from my hand!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.220
A Ritual Summon?

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:13.820
Yes. When you activate a Ritual Spell, you release the required Levels from your hand or field to Special Summon a Monster.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:17.860
I release the Level Four Photon Chargeman in my hand!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.320
Ritual Summon!

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:23.330
Come forth, Knight of Photon Dragon!

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:35.510
And by releasing Knight of Photon Dragon, I can Special Summon Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon from my hand or Deck!

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.550
Descend, Embodiment of Light!

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.680
Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:47.640
I use Galaxy-Eyes to attack Infection Baal Zeboul!

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:52.190
Did you forget, Kaito? Numbers can only be beaten by another Number!

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:53.860
You sure about that?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:54.440
What!?

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:56.690
I activate my Galaxy-Eyes' effect!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:17:01.610
When this Monster battles, it can Banish the opponent's Monster and itself!

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:03.620
Not good!

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:10.330
At that moment, if the Banished Monster is an Xyz, all of its Overlay Units are sent to the Graveyard.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:15.550
And the Monsters Banished by this effect return to the field when the battle ends.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:23.890
And then my Galaxy-Eyes that returned to the field gains 500 Attack Points for each Overlay Unit sent to the Graveyard!

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:30.600
Your Number can't activate its effects now that it has no Overlay Units!

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.900
NO!

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.360
Just kidding.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:41.700
Unfortunately, Kaito, I already have a winning formula to win.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.160
Hmph. Ripping off Astral, now?

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:47.330
I set one card face-down! Turn end!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.830
It's time for Hell's SHOWTIME!

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.750
I see I kept you waiting. What's up?

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:58.670
Why the hell did you guys call for an emergency meeting?

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:00.670
Huh?

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.600
Who's that?

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:08.310
Long time, no see, Vector.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.310
Who the hell are you?!

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:14.060
You forgot about us? How cruel.

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:17.520
I-It can't be...! She's Merag!

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:20.150
Th-Then the other one's...!?

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:30.120
Na...Nasch!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:35.580
It can't be... You're still alive!?

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.550
It's my turn! Draw!

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.760
Now here I come, Kaito!

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:43.760
Now watch carefully!

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.340
Infection Ball Zeboul...

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:50.220
Activate your effect!

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:55.400
Once per turn, I can make one Number monster in my opponent's Graveyard an Overlay Unit for this Monster!

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:56.350
What!?

00:18:56.350 --> 00:19:00.820
I'll make Shadow Mosquito an Overlay Unit for Baal Zeboul!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.860
Does it hurt?

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:09.910
But I won't accept a surrender.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:14.370
I'd rather die than surrender to you!

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:17.670
Very well. I'll make your wish come true.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.750
I activate Baal Zeboul's other effect!

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:26.720
Once per turn, by detaching an Overlay Unit, I can destroy one card my opponent controls!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:34.480
And if the destroyed card is a Monster Card, its Attack Points are inflicted to the player as damage!

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:39.480
I'll destroy Galaxy-Eyes!

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.520
Crap!

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:43.110
He's gonna take 4500 damage now!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.030
He'll wipe Kaito out in one hit!

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.360
Kaito!

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:49.070
This is the end for you!

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:53.040
I... I activate a Trap! Prevent Draw!

00:19:54.330 --> 00:20:00.920
When Effect Damage happens, I can halve that damage!

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:18.900
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.770
What power!

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:24.400
Is this the might of this Number that you were telling me about, Master Vector!?

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.610
III! V!

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:29.740
Throw away the Numbers you got from the Barians!

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:30.950
I'm certain.

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:43.130
Oh, throwing away Numbers? What a waste. Such a waste!

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:45.460
What the? That shock...

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.130
That Number...

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:52.930
The Power! Oh, the Numbers' Power!

00:20:55.770 --> 00:21:03.270
After Prevent Draw halves the Effect Damage... I can draw one... c... card...

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:08.190
Kaito!

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:11.240
My next Direct Attack will finish this!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:12.410
Kaito!

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.330
Stop right there, ya villainous scum!

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:19.870
That voice...!

00:21:58.700 --> 00:22:00.790
Yuma! Astral!

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:02.790
Hey, Kotori!

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:06.250
Now we're back!

00:22:21.210 --> 00:22:23.710
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:26.250
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:27.460
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:28.880
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:31.760
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:34.260
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:36.810
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:37.890
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:38.930
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:42.310
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.310 --> 00:22:44.650
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:47.780
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:49.990
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:52.990
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:54.950
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:54.950 --> 00:22:56.330
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:58.200
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.490 --> 00:23:02.500
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:07.590
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.590 --> 00:23:08.840
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:12.840
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.340 --> 00:23:18.220
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.220 --> 00:23:19.430
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:23.560
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.730
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:25.730 --> 00:23:27.940
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:42.890
Before Mr. Heartland and his shameless tricks,

00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:45.940
Kaito falls down while relaying his wish to his friends.

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:50.060
And we'll take over this Duel for him!

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:53.150
Is this how low you've fallen, Heartland?!

00:23:53.150 --> 00:23:56.320
I couldn't be happier fighting beside you again!

00:23:56.320 --> 00:23:58.780
The time has come for the Seven Barian Emperors to combine their strength!

00:23:58.780 --> 00:24:01.030
Yuma, let's win this Duel!

00:24:01.030 --> 00:24:03.160
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:06.000
"The Hero's Triumphant Return! Carrying On a Friend's Will!!"

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:09.000
This is the power of the evolved ZEXAL!
